  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Common Shelter and Non-Food Items (NFI) Pipeline for Flood Response in Northeast Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Floods are among the most devastating natural hazards in the world, claiming more lives and causing more property damage than any other natural phenomenon. With the onset of the rainy season in June in Nigeria, varying degrees of damage have been reported all over the country. The devastation caused by floods have significantly disrupted economic and social systems essential for livelihoods, social cohesion and individual well-being. This is against the backdrop of an ongoing conflict, which has resulted in the loss of human life, population displacement and destruction of productive assets, economic infrastructure and social services. IOM&apos;s strong operational presence in Borno and Yobe provides a strong operational advantage to provide a common pipeline through which emergency shelter solutions and non-food items can reach the communities that are affected by floods in Northeast Nigeria. This project is addressing immediate lifesaving needs of the displaced flood-affected populations who face heightened exposure to protection risks such as gender-based violence, exploitation and abuse as a result of loss of shelter and household items.</narrative>
  </description>
